---
import Terminal from '../layouts/Terminal.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const posts = (await getCollection('posts', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());

const fmt = (d: Date) =>
  d.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });

const toc = [
  { id: 'sec-present', label: 'Present' },
  { id: 'sec-past', label: 'Past' },
  { id: 'sec-posts', label: 'Posts' },
  { id: 'sec-projects', label: 'Projects' },
  { id: 'sec-personal', label: 'Hobbies and Interests' },
];
const dash40 = '─'.repeat(40);
---
<Terminal title="Sathvik Rajampalli" toc={toc}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Sathvik Rajampalli',
    email: 'vr2618@columbia.edu',
    affiliation: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'Columbia University' },
    jobTitle: 'MSEE Student',
    description: 'Researching hw–sw co-design, firmware, and computer (micro)architecture.',
  })} />

  <div class="prompt">
    <span class="ac">sathvik@columbia</span><span class="dm">:</span><span>~</span><span class="dm">$</span> ./whoami
  </div>

  <div class="fetch">
    <pre id="ascii"></pre>
    <div class="fetch-info">
      <div class="name">Sathvik Rajampalli</div>
      <div class="hr">{dash40}</div>
      <div class="kv">
        <span class="k">Role:</span><span>2nd-year MSEE student @ <strong>Columbia University</strong></span>
        <span class="k">Interests:</span><span>HW–SW co-design, Firmware, and Computer Architecture</span>
        <span class="k">Location:</span><span>New York, NY</span>
        <span class="k">Email:</span><span><a href="mailto:vr2618@columbia.edu">vr2618@columbia.edu</a></span>
        <span class="k">GitHub:</span><span><a href="https://github.com/7vik03" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/7vik03</a></span>
        <span class="k">LinkedIn:</span><span><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sathvik-rajampalli/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/in/sathvik-rajampalli</a></span>
        <span class="k">X:</span><span><a href="https://x.com/sathvikrjpl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/sathvikrjpl</a></span>
        <span class="k">Mastodon:</span><span><a href="https://mastodon.social/@gleibniz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@gleibniz</a></span>
        <span class="k">Resume:</span><span><a href="/resume.pdf">resume.pdf</a></span>
        <span class="k">Personal Quote:</span><span>"Everything is a finite state machine."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="palette-row">
        <span class="lab">Palette</span>
        <span class="dm" style="font-size:12px">›</span>
        {['#2e9e95','#3b82c4','#4caf6d','#d4638f','#e08a3c','#d1495b','#8b6fd1','#c9a227'].map((c) => (
          <button class="swatch" type="button" aria-label={`accent ${c}`} style={`background:${c}`}></button>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Section title="Present" id="sec-present">
    I'm currently a second-year MSEE student at <a href="https://www.columbia.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Columbia University</a>, focused on the boundary between software and hardware: writing software shaped around the microarchitecture it runs on, and designing hardware shaped around the software it needs to accelerate. My active research interest is architecture-aware algorithm design. A related interest of mine that hasn't yet materialized is hardware security.
    <div class="sub">Updates</div>
    <div class="rows">
      <span class="t">[summer '26]*</span><span>Researching microarchitecture-aware sparse tensor algebra for Apple Silicon, advised by <a href="#">Prof. Olivia Hsu</a> (CMU) and <a href="#">Prof. Martha Kim</a> (Columbia).</span>
      <span class="t">[spring '26]</span><span>Contributed to the high-level software design of a tile dispatcher system for a GPU backend, part of sparse tiling research led by <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=SFZbCC0AAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sai Gautham Ravipati</a> (Stanford) and <a href="#">Prof. Olivia Hsu</a> (CMU).</span>
      <span class="t">[fall '25]</span><span>Implemented dynamic voltage and frequency scaling (DVFS) algorithms for high-bandwidth memory (HBM) in Ramulator2, advised by <a href="https://takhandipu.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prof. Tanvir Ahmed Khan</a> (Columbia).</span>
      <span class="t">[fall '25]</span><span>Enrolled in the MSEE program at Columbia University.</span>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Past" id="sec-past">
    My path has been a slow fall down the stack, (high level) ML systems, then ML systems, and finally hardcore systems research. Each year a little closer to the metal, and a little harder to explain at parties.
    <br /><br />
    It all started with a B.Tech in ECE at <a href="#">VIT</a>.
    <div class="sub">Past roles</div>
    <div class="rows">
      <span class="t">[spring '25]</span><span><a href="#">Arcserve</a> — worked on document retrieval &amp; comparison tooling (FAISS, FLAN-T5/Llama).</span>
      <span class="t">[summer '24]</span><span><a href="#">Bhabha Atomic Research Centre</a> — worked on real-time face-recognition pipelines for continuous authentication.</span>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Posts" id="sec-posts" bodyClass="list">
    <div class="dm">$ ls ./posts</div>
    {posts.length === 0 ? (
      <div style="margin-top:10px" class="dm">Nothing here yet, check back soon.</div>
    ) : (
      <div class="postlist">
        {posts.map((p) => (
          <>
            <span class="d">[{fmt(p.data.date)}]</span>
            <a href={`/posts/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a>
          </>
        ))}
      </div>
    )}
    <div class="feedline">$ curl -s <a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a></div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Projects" id="sec-projects" bodyClass="list">
    <div><span class="ac">[gpu profiling, graphics]</span> CUDA Acceleration of Black Hole Ray Marching Visualization</div>
    <div><span class="ac">[fpga, hardware graphics]</span> Pipelined 16-Lane Systolic Pineda Triangle Rasterizer on DE1-SoC</div>
    <div><span class="ac">[computer architecture, rtl]</span> Out-of-Order Processor</div>
    <div><span class="ac">[operating systems]</span> tba</div>
    <div><span class="ac">[operating systems]</span> tba</div>
    <div><span class="ac">[operating systems]</span> tba</div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Hobbies and Interests" id="sec-personal" bodyClass="tight">
    <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
      <span class="t">•</span><span>Lifting weights. Have been lifting since junior year of undergrad, only to look just about average.</span>
      <span class="t">•</span><span>I love thinking and discussing about human psychology and behaviour. Both, academic and practical angles appeal to me, although, it is heavily skewed towards practical as of now.</span>
      <span class="t">•</span><span>Currently reading <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/10883.Benjamin_Franklin" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-style:italic">Benjamin Franklin</a> by Walter Isaacson.</span>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <div style="margin-top:30px; font-size:15px">
    <span class="ac">sathvik@columbia</span><span class="dm">:</span><span>~</span><span class="dm">$</span> <span class="caret"></span>
  </div>
</Terminal>
